# Zen Minimal Design Pivot

Based on user feedback, we are pivoting from "Celestial Dark" to a high-contrast, compact, and distraction-free "Zen Minimal" aesthetic.

## Proposed Changes

### [Global Styling]

#### [MODIFY] [index.css](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/index.css)
- Switch default color scheme to **Light Mode**.
- Use a crisp, high-contrast palette (White background, Slate-900 text).
- Define "Compact" spacing tokens.
- Replace heavy glassmorphism with subtle, refined borders and shadows.

### [Core Layout]

#### [MODIFY] [Layout.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/components/Layout.tsx)
- **Compact Sidebar**: Reduce width and internal padding.
- **Remove Clutter**: Delete system status, version indicators, and environment labels.
- **Tighten Navigation**: Reduce size of icons and gap between menu items.

### [UI Components]

#### [MODIFY] [Button.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/components/ui/Button.tsx)
- Standardize on light-mode variants (Solid dark for primary, light borders for secondary).
- Reduce vertical and horizontal padding for all sizes.

#### [MODIFY] [Card.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/components/ui/Card.tsx)
- Reduce default padding from `p-10+` to `p-6` or less.
- Use sharper, smaller border-radius (e.g., `rounded-xl`).
- Switch to high-contrast white backgrounds with subtle borders.

### [Feature Pages]

#### [MODIFY] [PlannerPage.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/pages/planner/PlannerPage.tsx)
- Collapse daily cards into more horizontal, space-efficient rows.
- Simplify meal slot display; remove decorative gradients.
- Increase information density.

#### [MODIFY] [ShoppingListPage.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/pages/planner/ShoppingListPage.tsx)
- Convert large cards into a dense list or table-like grid.
- Remove redundant labels like "Requirement" or "Acquired Entities".
- Simplify status toggles.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `npm run build` to verify Tailwind v4 bundle integrity.

### Manual Verification
1. Verify readability under different lighting conditions (Light mode check).
2. Measure information density: ensure more than 5 items are visible without scrolling on standard viewports.
3. Confirm absence of system/version text.
